{"id":"mahabharata-12-258","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":258,"title":"अष्टपञ्चाशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 258 · The slow-acting Chirakarin","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks how to judge an act, quickly or slowly, and Bhishma tells the story of Gautama's son Chirakarin, who was ordered by his father to kill his mother. Thinking long before he acted, he spared her, and his father, repenting, praised the slow-acting.","kn":"ಕೆಲಸವನ್ನು ಬೇಗ ಅಥವಾ ನಿಧಾನವಾಗಿ ಹೇಗೆ ವಿಚಾರಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ತಂದೆ ಗೌತಮ ತಾಯಿಯನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲಲು ಹೇಳಿದ ಮಗ ಚಿರಕಾರಿಕನ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಬಹುಕಾಲ ಯೋಚಿಸಿ ಅವನು ಅವಳನ್ನು ಉಳಿಸಿದ, ತಂದೆ ಪಶ್ಚಾತ್ತಾಪಪಟ್ಟು ನಿಧಾನವಾಗಿ ಮಾಡುವವನನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳಿದ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि कार्य को शीघ्रता से या देर से कैसे परखें, और भीष्म गौतम के पुत्र चिरकारिक की कथा सुनाते हैं जिसे पिता ने माता को मारने का आदेश दिया था। उसने देर तक सोचकर उसे बचा लिया और पिता ने पछताकर धीरे करने वाले की प्रशंसा की।","te":"పనిని త్వరగా లేదా ఆలస్యంగా ఎలా విచారించాలని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; తండ్రి గౌతముడు తల్లిని చంపమని ఆదేశించిన కుమారుడు చిరకారికుని కథను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. చాలాసేపు ఆలోచించి అతడు ఆమెను కాపాడాడు, తండ్రి పశ్చాత్తాపపడి నెమ్మదిగా చేసేవాణ్ని ప్రశంసించాడు.","ta":"செயலை விரைந்தோ தாமதித்தோ எவ்வாறு ஆராய வேண்டும் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, தந்தை கௌதமர் தாயைக் கொல்லுமாறு பணித்த மகன் சிரகாரிகனின் கதையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். நீண்டநேரம் யோசித்து அவன் அவளைக் காத்தான், தந்தை வருந்தி நிதானமாகச் செய்பவனைப் புகழ்ந்தார்.","ml":"ഒരു പ്രവൃത്തി വേഗത്തിലോ സാവധാനത്തിലോ വിലയിരുത്തേണ്ടതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; അമ്മയെ കൊല്ലാൻ പിതാവ് ആജ്ഞാപിച്ച ഗൗതമന്റെ പുത്രൻ ചിരകാരിന്റെ കഥ ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. പ്രവർത്തിക്കുന്നതിനുമുമ്പ് ദീർഘമായി ആലോചിച്ച അദ്ദേഹം അമ്മയെ വെറുതെവിട്ടു; പശ്ചാത്തപിച്ച പിതാവ് സാവധാനത്തിൽ പ്രവർത്തിക്കുന്നവനെ പ്രശംസിച്ചു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.258; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कथं कार्यं परीक्षेत शीघ्रं वाथ चिरेण वा ।\nसर्वथा कार्यदुर्गेऽस्मिन्भवान्नः परमो गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How should one examine a task, quickly or slowly? In this hard maze of duties you are our supreme teacher in every way."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nचिरकारेस्तु यत्पूर्वं वृत्तमाङ्गिरसे कुले ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this too they tell this ancient tale, about what once happened to Chirakarin in the line of Angiras."}},{"n":3,"text":"चिरकारिक भद्रं ते भद्रं ते चिरकारिक ।\nचिरकारी हि मेधावी नापराध्यति कर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Good luck to you, Chirakarin, good luck, Chirakarin! The slow-acting, wise man does not go wrong in his deeds.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"चिरकारी महाप्राज्ञो गौतमस्याभवत्सुतः ।\nचिरं हि सर्वकार्याणि समेक्षावान्प्रपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The very wise Chirakarin was the son of Gautama. A thoughtful man takes up every task only after long consideration."}},{"n":5,"text":"चिरं संचिन्तयन्नर्थांश्चिरं जाग्रच्चिरं स्वपन् ।\nचिरकार्याभिसंपत्तेश्चिरकारी तथोच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pondered matters long, stayed awake long and slept long, and because he was long in completing tasks he was called \"Chirakarin,\" the slow-acting one."}},{"n":6,"text":"अलसग्रहणं प्राप्तो दुर्मेधावी तथोच्यते ।\nबुद्धिलाघवयुक्तेन जनेनादीर्घदर्शिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"But people of light understanding and short sight, taking him for lazy, called him dull-witted."}},{"n":7,"text":"व्यभिचारे तु कस्मिंश्चिद्व्यतिक्रम्यापरान्सुतान् ।\nपित्रोक्तः कुपितेनाथ जहीमां जननीमिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, over some lapse, the angry father passed over his other sons and told him: \"Kill this mother of yours.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"स तथेति चिरेणोक्त्वा स्वभावाच्चिरकारिकः ।\nविमृश्य चिरकारित्वाच्चिन्तयामास वै चिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So be it\" after a long while, as was his nature, Chirakarin reflected slowly, and being slow-acting he thought for a long time."}},{"n":9,"text":"पितुराज्ञां कथं कुर्यां न हन्यां मातरं कथम् ।\nकथं धर्मच्छले नास्मिन्निमज्जेयमसाधुवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can I obey my father's order? How can I not kill my mother? How can I avoid sinking, like a wicked man, into this trap of dharma?"}},{"n":10,"text":"पितुराज्ञा परो धर्मः स्वधर्मो मातृरक्षणम् ।\nअस्वतन्त्रं च पुत्रत्वं किं नु मां नात्र पीडयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A father's command is the highest dharma, and protecting the mother is my own dharma. A son is not independent; how would this not torment me?"}},{"n":11,"text":"स्त्रियं हत्वा मातरं च को हि जातु सुखी भवेत् ।\nपितरं चाप्यवज्ञाय कः प्रतिष्ठामवाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who could ever be happy after killing a woman, his mother? And who disrespecting his father could find a footing?"}},{"n":12,"text":"अनवज्ञा पितुर्युक्ता धारणं मातृरक्षणम् ।\nयुक्तक्षमावुभावेतौ नातिवर्तेतमां कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not disregarding the father is proper, and protecting the mother is upholding her. Both are fitting and forgivable; how may I not transgress either?"}},{"n":13,"text":"पिता ह्यात्मानमाधत्ते जायायां जज्ञियामिति ।\nशीलचारित्रगोत्रस्य धारणार्थं कुलस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The father places himself in his wife, to be born again, to uphold the character, conduct, lineage and family."}},{"n":14,"text":"सोऽहमात्मा स्वयं पित्रा पुत्रत्वे प्रकृतः पुनः ।\nविज्ञानं मे कथं न स्याद्बुबुधे चात्मसंभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am that self, set by my father himself as a son. How should I lack understanding, when I know I am born of him?"}},{"n":15,"text":"जातकर्मणि यत्प्राह पिता यच्चोपकर्मणि ।\nपर्याप्तः स दृढीकारः पितुर्गौरवनिश्चये ॥","meaning":{"en":"What the father says at the birth rite and at the initiation is enough to establish the father's authority."}},{"n":16,"text":"गुरुरग्र्यः परो धर्मः पोषणाध्ययनाद्धितः ।\nपिता यदाह धर्मः स वेदेष्वपि सुनिश्चितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The teacher is foremost, the highest dharma, beneficial by nurture and instruction. What the father says as dharma is firmly settled even in the Vedas."}},{"n":17,"text":"प्रीतिमात्रं पितुः पुत्रः सर्वं पुत्रस्य वै पिता ।\nशरीरादीनि देयानि पिता त्वेकः प्रयच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son is only the father's pleasure, but the father is everything to the son. The body and more are to be given, and only the father gives them."}},{"n":18,"text":"तस्मात्पितुर्वचः कार्यं न विचार्यं कथंचन ।\nपातकान्यपि पूयन्ते पितुर्वचनकारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the father's word should be done without any deliberation. Even sins are cleansed in those who carry out the father's word."}},{"n":19,"text":"भोगे भाग्ये प्रसवने सर्वलोकनिदर्शने ।\nभर्त्रा चैव समायोगे सीमन्तोन्नयने तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In enjoyment, in fortune, in birth, in all that is shown to the world, in union with the husband, and in the parting of the hair rite,"}},{"n":20,"text":"पिता स्वर्गः पिता धर्मः पिता परमकं तपः ।\nपितरि प्रीतिमापन्ने सर्वाः प्रीयन्ति देवताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the father is heaven, the father is dharma, the father is the highest austerity. When the father is pleased, all the gods are pleased."}},{"n":21,"text":"आशिषस्ता भजन्त्येनं पुरुषं प्राह याः पिता ।\nनिष्कृतिः सर्वपापानां पिता यदभिनन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessings the father speaks attach to that man. Whatever the father approves is atonement for all sins."}},{"n":22,"text":"मुच्यते बन्धनात्पुष्पं फलं वृन्तात्प्रमुच्यते ।\nक्लिश्यन्नपि सुतस्नेहैः पिता स्नेहं न मुञ्चति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A flower is freed from its stalk, a fruit from its stem, but a father, though troubled by love for his sons, never gives up affection."}},{"n":23,"text":"एतद्विचिन्तितं तावत्पुत्रस्य पितृगौरवम् ।\nपिता ह्यल्पतरं स्थानं चिन्तयिष्यामि मातरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This much is thought on a son's reverence for his father. The father holds a lesser place; I will now think of the mother."}},{"n":24,"text":"यो ह्ययं मयि संघातो मर्त्यत्वे पाञ्चभौतिकः ।\nअस्य मे जननी हेतुः पावकस्य यथारणिः ।\nमाता देहारणिः पुंसां सर्वस्यार्तस्य निर्वृतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This body, made of the five elements, that I have as a mortal: my mother is its cause, as the fire-stick is of fire. The mother, the body's fire-stick, is the comfort of every suffering man."}},{"n":25,"text":"न च शोचति नाप्येनं स्थाविर्यमपकर्षति ।\nश्रिया हीनोऽपि यो गेहे अम्बेति प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He does not grieve, and old age does not drag him down, who, though fortuneless, comes home and says \"Mother.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"पुत्रपौत्रसमाकीर्णो जननीं यः समाश्रितः ।\nअपि वर्षशतस्यान्ते स द्विहायनवच्चरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who relies on his mother, though surrounded by sons and grandsons, will live to the end of a hundred years like a two-year-old child."}},{"n":27,"text":"समर्थं वासमर्थं वा कृशं वाप्यकृशं तथा ।\nरक्षत्येव सुतं माता नान्यः पोष्टा विधानतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether capable or incapable, thin or not thin, the mother protects her son; no one else nourishes him by rule."}},{"n":28,"text":"तदा स वृद्धो भवति यदा भवति दुःखितः ।\nतदा शून्यं जगत्तस्य यदा मात्रा वियुज्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One is old only when he is in distress; and the world is empty for him when he is parted from his mother."}},{"n":29,"text":"नास्ति मातृसमा छाया नास्ति मातृसमा गतिः ।\nनास्ति मातृसमं त्राणं नास्ति मातृसमा प्रपा ॥","meaning":{"en":"No shade is like a mother, no refuge is like a mother, no protection is like a mother, and no water-hut is like a mother."}},{"n":30,"text":"कुक्षिसंधारणाद्धात्री जननाज्जननी स्मृता ।\nअङ्गानां वर्धनादम्बा वीरसूत्वेन वीरसूः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She is called \"dhatri\" for bearing in the womb, \"janani\" for giving birth, \"amba\" for growing the limbs, and \"viraprasu\" for bearing heroes."}},{"n":31,"text":"शिशोः शुश्रूषणाच्छुश्रूर्माता देहमनन्तरम् ।\nचेतनावान्नरो हन्याद्यस्य नासुषिरं शिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She is \"shushru\" for tending the infant, and the mother gives the body. A sensible man would kill one whose head is not hollow."}},{"n":32,"text":"दम्पत्योः प्राणसंश्लेषे योऽभिसंधिः कृतः किल ।\nतं माता वा पिता वेद भूतार्थो मातरि स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The intention formed at the joining of the couple's life-breaths is known by the mother or the father; the true matter rests in the mother."}},{"n":33,"text":"माता जानाति यद्गोत्रं माता जानाति यस्य सः ।\nमातुर्भरणमात्रेण प्रीतिः स्नेहः पितुः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mother knows the clan, and knows whose he is. Through the mother's mere support come the father's love, affection and children."}},{"n":34,"text":"पाणिबन्धं स्वयं कृत्वा सहधर्ममुपेत्य च ।\nयदि याप्यन्ति पुरुषाः स्त्रियो नार्हन्ति याप्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If men, having taken the wife's hand and entered on shared dharma, then cast them off, women do not deserve to be cast off."}},{"n":35,"text":"भरणाद्धि स्त्रियो भर्ता पात्याच्चैव स्त्रियाः पतिः ।\nगुणस्यास्य निवृत्तौ तु न भर्ता न पतिः पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The husband is \"bhartr\" for supporting the wife and \"pati\" for protecting her; when this quality ceases, he is neither bhartr nor pati."}},{"n":36,"text":"एवं स्त्री नापराध्नोति नर एवापराध्यति ।\nव्युच्चरंश्च महादोषं नर एवापराध्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus a woman does not offend; it is the man who offends. Straying, the man commits the great fault."}},{"n":37,"text":"स्त्रिया हि परमो भर्ता दैवतं परमं स्मृतम् ।\nतस्यात्मना तु सदृशमात्मानं परमं ददौ ।\nसर्वकार्यापराध्यत्वान्नापराध्यन्ति चाङ्गनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a woman the husband is the highest, the highest deity. He gave her an equal self to his own self. Women are not at fault, since all blame rests on the man."}},{"n":38,"text":"यश्चनोक्तो हि निर्देशः स्त्रिया मैथुनतृप्तये ।\nतस्य स्मारयतो व्यक्तमधर्मो नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The directive said of a woman for the satisfaction of intercourse, if one reminds her of it plainly, is unrighteous; there is no doubt."}},{"n":39,"text":"यावन्नारीं मातरं च गौरवे चाधिके स्थिताम् ।\nअवध्यां तु विजानीयुः पशवोऽप्यविचक्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even unintelligent animals know a woman and a mother, set in higher respect, to be not for killing."}},{"n":40,"text":"देवतानां समावायमेकस्थं पितरं विदुः ।\nमर्त्यानां देवतानां च स्नेहादभ्येति मातरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They know the father as an assembly of gods in one; but among mortals and gods, one goes to the mother out of love."}},{"n":41,"text":"एवं विमृशतस्तस्य चिरकारितया बहु ।\nदीर्घः कालो व्यतिक्रान्तस्ततस्तस्यागमत्पिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he thus reflected at length, in his slow way, a long time passed, and then his father came."}},{"n":42,"text":"मेधातिथिर्महाप्राज्ञो गौतमस्तपसि स्थितः ।\nविमृश्य तेन कालेन पत्न्याः संस्थाव्यतिक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The very wise Gautama Medhatithi, steady in austerity, after some time reflected on his wife's lapse from restraint."}},{"n":43,"text":"सोऽब्रवीद्दुःखसंतप्तो भृशमश्रूणि वर्तयन् ।\nश्रुतधैर्यप्रसादेन पश्चात्तापमुपागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tormented with grief, shedding many tears, and filled with remorse, through the grace of learning and steadiness, he said:"}},{"n":44,"text":"आश्रमं मम संप्राप्तस्त्रिलोकेशः पुरंदरः ।\nअतिथिव्रतमास्थाय ब्राह्मणं रूपमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Indra, lord of the three worlds, came to my hermitage in the form of a brahmin, keeping the guest vow."}},{"n":45,"text":"समया सान्त्वितो वाग्भिः स्वागतेनाभिपूजितः ।\nअर्घ्यं पाद्यं च न्यायेन तयाभिप्रतिपादितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She comforted him with kind words, honored him with welcome, and offered the water for arghya and for his feet properly."}},{"n":46,"text":"परवत्यस्मि चाप्युक्तः प्रणयिष्ये नयेन च ।\nअत्र चाकुशले जाते स्त्रियो नास्ति व्यतिक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She was told: 'I am under another's power,' and will 'win by gentleness'; and when wrong came of this, the woman did not transgress."}},{"n":47,"text":"एवं न स्त्री न चैवाहं नाध्वगस्त्रिदशेश्वरः ।\nअपराध्यति धर्मस्य प्रमादस्त्वपराध्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"So neither the woman, nor I, nor the traveler, lord of the thirty gods, is at fault; it is heedlessness of dharma that errs."}},{"n":48,"text":"ईर्ष्याजं व्यसनं प्राहुस्तेन चैवोर्ध्वरेतसः ।\nईर्ष्यया त्वहमाक्षिप्तो मग्नो दुष्कृतसागरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"They call calamity born of jealousy, and so too for those who hold their seed. Struck by jealousy I sank in an ocean of wrongdoing."}},{"n":49,"text":"हत्वा साध्वीं च नारीं च व्यसनित्वाच्च शासिताम् ।\nभर्तव्यत्वेन भार्यां च को नु मां तारयिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed a virtuous woman, punished through my own folly, my wife whom I should have supported, who will rescue me?"}},{"n":50,"text":"अन्तरेण मयाज्ञप्तश्चिरकारी ह्युदारधीः ।\nयद्यद्य चिरकारी स्यात्स मां त्रायेत पातकात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I commanded the noble-minded Chirakarin in secret. If he is slow today, he may save me from the sin."}},{"n":51,"text":"चिरकारिक भद्रं ते भद्रं ते चिरकारिक ।\nयद्यद्य चिरकारी त्वं ततोऽसि चिरकारिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chirakarin, good luck to you! If you are slow today, then you are truly Chirakarin."}},{"n":52,"text":"त्राहि मां मातरं चैव तपो यच्चार्जितं मया ।\nआत्मानं पातकेभ्यश्च भवाद्य चिरकारिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Save me, your mother and the austerity I have earned, and yourself from the sins. Be slow today."}},{"n":53,"text":"सहजं चिरकारित्वं चिरप्राज्ञतया तव ।\nसफलं तत्तवाद्यास्तु भवाद्य चिरकारिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your slowness is innate, from long-considering wisdom. May it prove fruitful today; be slow today."}},{"n":54,"text":"चिरमाशंसितो मात्रा चिरं गर्भेण धारितः ।\nसफलं चिरकारित्वं कुरु त्वं चिरकारिक ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long wished for by your mother, long borne in the womb, make your slowness fruitful, Chirakarin."}},{"n":55,"text":"चिरायते च संतापाच्चिरं स्वपिति वारितः ।\nआवयोश्चिरसंतापादवेक्ष्य चिरकारिक ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is slow from sorrow and sleeps long when stopped; look to our long suffering, Chirakarin.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"एवं स दुःखितो राजन्महर्षिर्गौतमस्तदा ।\nचिरकारिं ददर्शाथ पुत्रं स्थितमथान्तिके ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus grieving, O king, the great sage Gautama then saw his son Chirakarin standing near."}},{"n":57,"text":"चिरकारी तु पितरं दृष्ट्वा परमदुःखितः ।\nशस्त्रं त्यक्त्वा ततो मूर्ध्ना प्रसादायोपचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chirakarin, seeing his father, greatly distressed, threw down the weapon and began to appease him, bowing his head."}},{"n":58,"text":"गौतमस्तु सुतं दृष्ट्वा शिरसा पतितं भुवि ।\nपत्नीं चैव निराकारां परामभ्यगमन्मुदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gautama, seeing his son fallen head to the ground, and his wife without form, felt great joy."}},{"n":59,"text":"न हि सा तेन संभेदं पत्नी नीता महात्मना ।\nविजने चाश्रमस्थेन पुत्रश्चापि समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That wife had not been led into any union by that great-souled man; and the son too, in a lonely hermitage, was composed."}},{"n":60,"text":"हन्यात्त्वनपवादेन शस्त्रपाणौ सुते स्थिते ।\nविनीतं प्रश्नयित्वा च व्यवस्येदात्मकर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"He might kill the blameless one, with the son standing weapon in hand; but a disciplined man, having questioned, should settle on his own acts."}},{"n":61,"text":"बुद्धिश्चासीत्सुतं दृष्ट्वा पितुश्चरणयोर्नतम् ।\nशस्त्रग्रहणचापल्यं संवृणोति भयादिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"On seeing his son bowed at his father's feet, it occurred to Gautama that the rashness of taking up the weapon was restrained by fear."}},{"n":62,"text":"ततः पित्रा चिरं स्तुत्वा चिरं चाघ्राय मूर्धनि ।\nचिरं दोर्भ्यां परिष्वज्य चिरं जीवेत्युदाहृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the father praised him long, smelled his head long, embraced him long with his arms, and said, \"Live long.\""}},{"n":63,"text":"एवं स गौतमः पुत्रं प्रीतिहर्षसमन्वितः ।\nअभिनन्द्य महाप्राज्ञ इदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So Gautama, full of love and joy, embraced his son and, wise as he was, said this:"}},{"n":64,"text":"चिरकारिक भद्रं ते चिरकारी चिरं भव ।\nचिरायमाणे त्वयि च चिरमस्मि सुदुःखितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Chirakarin, good luck to you; be slow-acting long. While you were slow I was deeply distressed for long.\""}},{"n":65,"text":"गाथाश्चाप्यब्रवीद्विद्वान्गौतमो मुनिसत्तमः ।\nचिरकारिषु धीरेषु गुणोद्देशसमाश्रयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the learned Gautama, best of sages, spoke verses about the steady slow-acting, drawing on the praise of their qualities."}},{"n":66,"text":"चिरेण मित्रं बध्नीयाच्चिरेण च कृतं त्यजेत् ।\nचिरेण हि कृतं मित्रं चिरं धारणमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Slowly one should make a friend, and slowly give up one made; a friend made slowly deserves to be kept long."}},{"n":67,"text":"रागे दर्पे च माने च द्रोहे पापे च कर्मणि ।\nअप्रिये चैव कर्तव्ये चिरकारी प्रशस्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In passion, pride, conceit, malice, sinful deeds and in doing what is disagreeable, the slow-acting man is praised."}},{"n":68,"text":"बन्धूनां सुहृदां चैव भृत्यानां स्त्रीजनस्य च ।\nअव्यक्तेष्वपराधेषु चिरकारी प्रशस्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Toward kinsmen, friends, servants and women, in unproven offenses, the slow-acting man is praised."}},{"n":69,"text":"एवं स गौतमस्तस्य प्रीतः पुत्रस्य भारत ।\nकर्मणा तेन कौरव्य चिरकारितया तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"So Gautama, pleased, Bharata, O Kaurava, with that deed of his son and that slowness of his,"}},{"n":70,"text":"एवं सर्वेषु कार्येषु विमृश्य पुरुषस्ततः ।\nचिरेण निश्चयं कृत्वा चिरं न परितप्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"so a man who deliberates in all affairs and decides slowly does not long suffer remorse."}},{"n":71,"text":"चिरं धारयते रोषं चिरं कर्म नियच्छति ।\nपश्चात्तापकरं कर्म न किंचिदुपपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He holds his anger long, restrains his deeds long, and no deed that brings regret comes to him."}},{"n":72,"text":"चिरं वृद्धानुपासीत चिरमन्वास्य पूजयेत् ।\nचिरं धर्मान्निषेवेत कुर्याच्चान्वेषणं चिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should long attend the elders, long sit by them and honor them, long practice dharma, and long make inquiry."}},{"n":73,"text":"चिरमन्वास्य विदुषश्चिरं शिष्टान्निषेव्य च ।\nचिरं विनीय चात्मानं चिरं यात्यनवज्ञताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having long served the learned and long attended the good, and having long disciplined himself, he is long free from contempt."}},{"n":74,"text":"ब्रुवतश्च परस्यापि वाक्यं धर्मोपसंहितम् ।\nचिरं पृच्छेच्चिरं ब्रूयाच्चिरं न परिभूयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even to another's words joined with dharma, he should long ask, long answer, and so is not long despised."}},{"n":75,"text":"उपास्य बहुलास्तस्मिन्नाश्रमे सुमहातपाः ।\nसमाः स्वर्गं गतो विप्रः पुत्रेण सहितस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having dwelt many years in that hermitage in great austerity, the brahmin then went to heaven together with his son."}}]}]}